{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RDw3p3gGMF1ACvpXU9YZUB","type":"tool_result","content":"e69de29bb2d1d6434b8b29ae775ad8c2e48c5391\n80316a42 chore(pose): bind the vread matrix to its review\ne6e8e55c chore(pose): index the vread matrix\n61e0ba78 chore(pose): record the vread matrix\n6f9dae10 chore(pose): index the vread round r3 fixes\n4f87b0af fix(pose): keep the index's time on its read-only copy and read plainly without an index\n29ff6c69 chore(pose): record review round 2 of the validate-reads spec\n593be875 chore(pose): index the vread binding\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\nindex 39ed6ba5..2b3f7198 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ If Git stopped skipping a failed refresh lock silently, the diff would fail inst\n \n ### Decision D1\n - Basis: R1\n-R1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` (enough for `git status`), and a diff against the work tree runs unchanged but reads the index through `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/N`, an anonymous memory file (`memfd`) holding the index's bytes. Git resolves that link to `/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)`, cannot create its lock beside it (the directory does not exist, for any user), and skips the refresh write silently, so the answer is the plain diff's and nothing is written. Two earlier versions were refused: a private copy of the index in a temporary file, by the full suite (a dry run creates no file, `TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`); and answers rebuilt from `git status`, by review round 1, which found five states they got wrong (submodules ignored by configuration, conflicts, symlinks, a POSE root below the repository top). Outside Linux the copy is used (L2).\n+R1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` (enough for `git status`), and a diff against the work tree runs unchanged but reads the index through `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/N`, an anonymous memory file (`memfd`) holding the index's bytes. Git resolves that link to `/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)`, cannot create its lock beside it (the directory does not exist, for any user), and skips the refresh write silently, so the answer is the plain diff's and nothing is written. The memory file keeps the index's modification time, because Git trusts an entry's stat only when its file is older than the index: a fresher copy would hide a change made in the index's own second. A repository without an index file reads plainly, as there is no stat cache to write. Two earlier versions were refused: a private copy of the index in a temporary file, by the full suite (a dry run creates no file, `TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`); and answers rebuilt from `git status`, by review round 1, which found five states they got wrong (submodules ignored by configuration, conflicts, symlinks, a POSE root below the repository top). Outside Linux the copy is used (L2).\n \n ### Decision D2\n - Basis: R3\n@@ -113,12 +113,13 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n - 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-b249b5d958a5d8ff) requested changes with N1–N9: the status-based answers differed from `git diff` for a submodule ignored by `.gitmodules`, a submodule with uncommitted content, symlinks and a directory replaced by a file, unmerged entries, a POSE root below the repository top, intent-to-add, staged-then-reverted changes and a range base. They were withdrawn: the callers run their original `git diff` again, reading the index through a `memfd` (D1). `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff` builds those states and requires each read to answer byte for byte as the plain diff, leave `.git/index` identical and leave no lock; it also runs the review history ledger's diff (N9). Each guard fails its test mutated out.\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 2 (rrn-233e9d0e27a7230a) requested changes. N10: the memfd carried a new time, so a racily clean entry was trusted on its stat and a real change was hidden; the memfd (and the copy outside Linux) now keeps the index's modification time, and `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry` fails with the current time in its place. N11: without an index file the read runs plainly instead of failing, and `check` applies the read-only index to its diff only (`TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex` fails with the missing-index case removed; the diff-only restriction is behaviour-preserving, as `ls-files` never writes, and has no test of its own). N13: scope selection keeps the cause of a failed read, and the index read reports its own error. N12 is a follow-up.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n-- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry, test:TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex\n - R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n \n@@ -140,4 +141,4 @@ The engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite\n L1 and L2 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-None.\n+- [open] Keep a split-index read from touching the modification time of `.git/sharedindex.<hash>`, which Git updates when it reads the shared index (review round 2, N12). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\nindex cbe26ac8..6442799f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n@@ -1134,10 +1134,13 @@ func (checker *nativeChecker) readyTransitionCandidates() []string {\n \t\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n \t\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n \t\tcmd := pose.RawHistoryGit(checker.root, command...)\n-\t\tdone, err := pose.ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, checker.root)\n-\t\tif err != nil {\n-\t\t\tdone()\n-\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\tdone := func() {}\n+\t\tif command[0] == \"diff\" {\n+\t\t\tvar err error\n+\t\t\tif done, err = pose.ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, checker.root); err != nil {\n+\t\t\t\tdone()\n+\t\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t\toutput, err := cmd.Output()\n \t\tdone()\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex 8f26fbd0..35058442 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -300,7 +300,13 @@ func reportChangedFiles(root, since string) []string {\n \t}\n \t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n \t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n-\toutput, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\tvar output []byte\n+\tvar err error\n+\tif since != \"\" {\n+\t\toutput, err = posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\t} else {\n+\t\toutput, err = posemodel.RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t}\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\nindex 663b28a7..044adad7 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ import (\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n \t\"sync\"\n \t\"testing\"\n \t\"time\"\n@@ -119,3 +120,30 @@ func TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex(t *testing.T) {\n \tdefault:\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Review round 2, N11: without an index file the reads still answer: the\n+// untracked spec is a ready-transition candidate and the report lists it.\n+func TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, _ := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tif err := os.Remove(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"specs\", \"2026-11-26-beta.md\"), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfound := false\n+\tfor _, c := range (&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates() {\n+\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(c, \"2026-11-26-beta.md\") {\n+\t\t\tfound = true\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif !found {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the ready transition read lost the new spec without an index\")\n+\t}\n+\tif files := reportChangedFiles(root, \"\"); len(files) == 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"report listed nothing without an index\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{}); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scope selection failed without an index: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex d4b2c6e2..83000ea6 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n \tout, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, gitArgs...)\n \tif err != nil {\n-\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?)\", sel.rangeLabel())\n+\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?): %v\", sel.rangeLabel(), err)\n \t}\n \tfor _, name := range strings.Split(string(out), \"\\x00\") {\n \t\tif name != \"\" {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nindex a9dbd243..ac39ecd0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ package pose\n \n import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"strings\"\n )\n@@ -26,11 +27,28 @@ func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n-\traw, err := readBoundedRegular(strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\"), diffIndexLimit)\n+\tpath := strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\")\n+\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n+\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\t\t// No index yet: there is no stat cache to refresh, so the plain read\n+\t\t// writes nothing (review round 2, N11).\n+\t\treturn func() {}, nil\n+\t}\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif !info.Mode().IsRegular() || info.Size() > diffIndexLimit {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is not a regular file within %d bytes\", root, diffIndexLimit)\n+\t}\n+\traw, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n-\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw)\n+\t// The copy keeps the index's modification time: Git trusts an entry on\n+\t// its stat only when the file is older than the index, so a fresher copy\n+\t// would hide a change made in the index's own second (review round 2,\n+\t// N10, racy-clean entries).\n+\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw, info.ModTime())\n }\n \n // RawGitDiffReadOnly runs RawGit(args...), a diff of the repository at root,\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\nindex 05ef93ed..bcc6e8fd 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"time\"\n \n \t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n )\n@@ -15,7 +16,7 @@ import (\n // and tries to create its lock next to it, in a directory that does not\n // exist, so the lock fails for any user, root included, and the refresh is\n // not written. No file is created.\n-func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte, modTime time.Time) (func(), error) {\n \tfd, err := unix.MemfdCreate(\"pose-index/none\", unix.MFD_CLOEXEC)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: an in-memory index cannot be made: %w\", err)\n@@ -29,6 +30,11 @@ func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n \t\tf.Close()\n \t\treturn func() {}, err\n \t}\n+\tts := unix.NsecToTimespec(modTime.UnixNano())\n+\tif err := unix.UtimesNanoAt(unix.AT_FDCWD, fmt.Sprintf(\"/proc/self/fd/%d\", fd), []unix.Timespec{ts, ts}, 0); err != nil {\n+\t\tf.Close()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the in-memory index cannot keep the index's time: %w\", err)\n+\t}\n \tcmd.ExtraFiles = append(cmd.ExtraFiles, f)\n \tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, fmt.Sprintf(\"GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/%d\", 2+len(cmd.ExtraFiles)))\n \treturn func() { f.Close() }, nil\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\nindex 1b633784..6cb7e722 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_other.go\n@@ -6,11 +6,12 @@ import (\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"time\"\n )\n \n // readOnlyIndexFor hands raw to cmd as a private copy: Git refreshes and may\n // rewrite the copy, never the checkout's index.\n-func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte, modTime time.Time) (func(), error) {\n \tdir, err := os.MkdirTemp(\"\", \"pose-index-*\")\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, err\n@@ -21,6 +22,10 @@ func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n \t\tdone()\n \t\treturn func() {}, err\n \t}\n+\tif err := os.Chtimes(path, modTime, modTime); err != nil {\n+\t\tdone()\n+\t\treturn func() {}, err\n+\t}\n \t// A split index would write a new shared index into .git.\n \tcmd.Args = append([]string{cmd.Args[0], \"-c\", \"core.splitIndex=false\"}, cmd.Args[1:]...)\n \tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, \"GIT_INDEX_FILE=\"+path)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\nindex fbe9c788..4f071acb 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_test.go\n@@ -140,3 +140,45 @@ func TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff(t *testing.T) {\n \t\t}\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Review round 2, N10: an entry racily clean against the index (its file as\n+// new as the index) is still compared by content: the copy keeps the index's\n+// time, so Git does not trust the stat a fresher copy would make old.\n+func TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot := t.TempDir()\n+\tgit := func(args ...string) {\n+\t\tt.Helper()\n+\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\"}, args...)...).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(args, err, string(out))\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"init\", \"-q\")\n+\tfile := filepath.Join(root, \"a.txt\")\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(file, []byte(\"aaaa\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\t// An old file time, so the entry is written clean, not smudged as racy.\n+\tstamp := time.Now().Add(-time.Hour).Truncate(time.Second)\n+\tif err := os.Chtimes(file, stamp, stamp); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tgit(\"add\", \"a.txt\")\n+\tgit(\"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"i\")\n+\t// Same size, same time: only the content tells the change.\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(file, []byte(\"bbbb\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, p := range []string{file, filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")} {\n+\t\tif err := os.Chtimes(p, stamp, stamp); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\targs := []string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"core.trustctime=false\", \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--\"}\n+\tgot, err := RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif string(got) != \"a.txt\\n\" {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a racily clean change was hidden: %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-abbeef1ba0/claude-review/tmp/claude-1000\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-abbeef1ba0/claude-review/tmp\n/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-ready","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"e9df8d8b-d31f-4f8e-95ab-3ccad60708b3","timestamp":"2026-11-26T16:57:19.315Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"e69de29bb2d1d6434b8b29ae775ad8c2e48c5391\n80316a42 chore(pose): bind the vread matrix to its review\ne6e8e55c chore(pose): index the vread matrix\n61e0ba78 chore(pose): record the vread matrix\n6f9dae10 chore(pose): index the vread round r3 fixes\n4f87b0af fix(pose): keep the index's time on its read-only copy and read plainly without an index\n29ff6c69 chore(pose): record review round 2 of the validate-reads spec\n593be875 chore(pose): index the vread binding\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\nindex 39ed6ba5..2b3f7198 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone.md\n@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ If Git stopped skipping a failed refresh lock silently, the diff would fail inst\n \n ### Decision D1\n - Basis: R1\n-R1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` (enough for `git status`), and a diff against the work tree runs unchanged but reads the index through `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/N`, an anonymous memory file (`memfd`) holding the index's bytes. Git resolves that link to `/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)`, cannot create its lock beside it (the directory does not exist, for any user), and skips the refresh write silently, so the answer is the plain diff's and nothing is written. Two earlier versions were refused: a private copy of the index in a temporary file, by the full suite (a dry run creates no file, `TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`); and answers rebuilt from `git status`, by review round 1, which found five states they got wrong (submodules ignored by configuration, conflicts, symlinks, a POSE root below the repository top). Outside Linux the copy is used (L2).\n+R1 as drafted asked for `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false`. Measured on a stale stat cache, `git diff --name-only HEAD` rewrites the index even with `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, and with `diff.autoRefreshIndex=false` it lists a file whose stat alone changed, which breaks the constraint that reads keep their results. So every engine Git command carries `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` (enough for `git status`), and a diff against the work tree runs unchanged but reads the index through `GIT_INDEX_FILE=/proc/self/fd/N`, an anonymous memory file (`memfd`) holding the index's bytes. Git resolves that link to `/memfd:pose-index/none (deleted)`, cannot create its lock beside it (the directory does not exist, for any user), and skips the refresh write silently, so the answer is the plain diff's and nothing is written. The memory file keeps the index's modification time, because Git trusts an entry's stat only when its file is older than the index: a fresher copy would hide a change made in the index's own second. A repository without an index file reads plainly, as there is no stat cache to write. Two earlier versions were refused: a private copy of the index in a temporary file, by the full suite (a dry run creates no file, `TestUpdatePreviewHasNoPhysicalMutationEvents`); and answers rebuilt from `git status`, by review round 1, which found five states they got wrong (submodules ignored by configuration, conflicts, symlinks, a POSE root below the repository top). Outside Linux the copy is used (L2).\n \n ### Decision D2\n - Basis: R3\n@@ -113,12 +113,13 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-26: `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` in `gitCommandContext`; the work-tree diffs of the ready-transition read, scope selection, `report --since` and the review history ledger read `git status` (`WorktreeChanges`, `WorktreeChangedNames`). `TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone`, `TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex` and `TestWorktreeReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone` fail with each guard mutated out (the optional-locks setting, each caller's `git diff` restored, the content comparison); the last also checks the answers equal `git diff` for a commit since the base, a modified, a deleted and a staged-new file. A first private-index version was refused by the full suite (D1).\n - 2026-11-26: review round 1 (rrn-b249b5d958a5d8ff) requested changes with N1–N9: the status-based answers differed from `git diff` for a submodule ignored by `.gitmodules`, a submodule with uncommitted content, symlinks and a directory replaced by a file, unmerged entries, a POSE root below the repository top, intent-to-add, staged-then-reverted changes and a range base. They were withdrawn: the callers run their original `git diff` again, reading the index through a `memfd` (D1). `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff` builds those states and requires each read to answer byte for byte as the plain diff, leave `.git/index` identical and leave no lock; it also runs the review history ledger's diff (N9). Each guard fails its test mutated out.\n+- 2026-11-26: review round 2 (rrn-233e9d0e27a7230a) requested changes. N10: the memfd carried a new time, so a racily clean entry was trusted on its stat and a real change was hidden; the memfd (and the copy outside Linux) now keeps the index's modification time, and `TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry` fails with the current time in its place. N11: without an index file the read runs plainly instead of failing, and `check` applies the read-only index to its diff only (`TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex` fails with the missing-index case removed; the diff-only restriction is behaviour-preserving, as `ls-files` never writes, and has no test of its own). N13: scope selection keeps the cause of a failed read, and the index read reports its own error. N12 is a follow-up.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n \n ### Requirement trace\n-- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff\n+- R1 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffAnswersAsThePlainDiff, test:TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry, test:TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex\n - R2 [satisfied] test:TestValidationReadsLeaveTheIndexAlone\n - R3 [satisfied] test:TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex\n \n@@ -140,4 +141,4 @@ The engine's Git reads during `validate`, `check` and `report` no longer rewrite\n L1 and L2 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-None.\n+- [open] Keep a split-index read from touching the modification time of `.git/sharedindex.<hash>`, which Git updates when it reads the shared index (review round 2, N12). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-26)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\nindex cbe26ac8..6442799f 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\n@@ -1134,10 +1134,13 @@ func (checker *nativeChecker) readyTransitionCandidates() []string {\n \t\t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n \t\t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n \t\tcmd := pose.RawHistoryGit(checker.root, command...)\n-\t\tdone, err := pose.ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, checker.root)\n-\t\tif err != nil {\n-\t\t\tdone()\n-\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\tdone := func() {}\n+\t\tif command[0] == \"diff\" {\n+\t\t\tvar err error\n+\t\t\tif done, err = pose.ReadOnlyIndex(cmd, checker.root); err != nil {\n+\t\t\t\tdone()\n+\t\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t\t}\n \t\t}\n \t\toutput, err := cmd.Output()\n \t\tdone()\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex 8f26fbd0..35058442 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -300,7 +300,13 @@ func reportChangedFiles(root, since string) []string {\n \t}\n \t// The diff reads the index without writing it (spec\n \t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n-\toutput, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\tvar output []byte\n+\tvar err error\n+\tif since != \"\" {\n+\t\toutput, err = posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, args...)\n+\t} else {\n+\t\toutput, err = posemodel.RawGit(args...).Output()\n+\t}\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn nil\n \t}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\nindex 663b28a7..044adad7 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\n@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@ import (\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n \t\"sync\"\n \t\"testing\"\n \t\"time\"\n@@ -119,3 +120,30 @@ func TestConcurrentValidationReadsNeverChangeTheIndex(t *testing.T) {\n \tdefault:\n \t}\n }\n+\n+// Review round 2, N11: without an index file the reads still answer: the\n+// untracked spec is a ready-transition candidate and the report lists it.\n+func TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex(t *testing.T) {\n+\troot, _ := staleIndexRepo(t)\n+\tif err := os.Remove(filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \".pose\", \"specs\", \"2026-11-26-beta.md\"), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfound := false\n+\tfor _, c := range (&nativeChecker{root: root}).readyTransitionCandidates() {\n+\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(c, \"2026-11-26-beta.md\") {\n+\t\t\tfound = true\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif !found {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"the ready transition read lost the new spec without an index\")\n+\t}\n+\tif files := reportChangedFiles(root, \"\"); len(files) == 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(\"report listed nothing without an index\")\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{}); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"scope selection failed without an index: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex d4b2c6e2..83000ea6 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \t// pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone R1).\n \tout, err := posemodel.RawGitDiffReadOnly(root, gitArgs...)\n \tif err != nil {\n-\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?)\", sel.rangeLabel())\n+\t\treturn sel, fmt.Errorf(\"git diff %s failed (revision unknown?): %v\", sel.rangeLabel(), err)\n \t}\n \tfor _, name := range strings.Split(string(out), \"\\x00\") {\n \t\tif name != \"\" {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\nindex a9dbd243..ac39ecd0 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ package pose\n \n import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n \t\"strings\"\n )\n@@ -26,11 +27,28 @@ func ReadOnlyIndex(cmd *exec.Cmd, root string) (func(), error) {\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be located: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n-\traw, err := readBoundedRegular(strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\"), diffIndexLimit)\n+\tpath := strings.TrimSuffix(string(out), \"\\n\")\n+\tinfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n+\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n+\t\t// No index yet: there is no stat cache to refresh, so the plain read\n+\t\t// writes nothing (review round 2, N11).\n+\t\treturn func() {}, nil\n+\t}\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif !info.Mode().IsRegular() || info.Size() > diffIndexLimit {\n+\t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s is not a regular file within %d bytes\", root, diffIndexLimit)\n+\t}\n+\traw, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the index of %s cannot be read: %w\", root, err)\n \t}\n-\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw)\n+\t// The copy keeps the index's modification time: Git trusts an entry on\n+\t// its stat only when the file is older than the index, so a fresher copy\n+\t// would hide a change made in the index's own second (review round 2,\n+\t// N10, racy-clean entries).\n+\treturn readOnlyIndexFor(cmd, raw, info.ModTime())\n }\n \n // RawGitDiffReadOnly runs RawGit(args...), a diff of the repository at root,\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\nindex 05ef93ed..bcc6e8fd 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\n@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ import (\n \t\"fmt\"\n \t\"os\"\n \t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"time\"\n \n \t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n )\n@@ -15,7 +16,7 @@ import (\n // and tries to create its lock next to it, in a directory that does not\n // exist, so the lock fails for any user, root included, and the refresh is\n // not written. No file is created.\n-func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n+func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte, modTime time.Time) (func(), error) {\n \tfd, err := unix.MemfdCreate(\"pose-index/none\", unix.MFD_CLOEXEC)\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn func() {}, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: an in-memory index cannot be made: %w\", err)\n@@ -29,6 +30,11 @@ func readOnlyIndexFor(cmd *exec.Cmd, raw []byte) (func(), error) {\n \t\tf.Close()\n \t\treturn func() {}, err\n \t}\n+\tts := unix.NsecToTimespec(modTime.UnixNano())\n+\tif err := unix.UtimesNanoAt(unix.AT_F