ft because both required `validate` tools failed, and I won't record a failed run as passed. No code change is needed for this; a rerun needs an environment where `validate --strict` can pass.\n\n## Validation failure\n- **Results:** the full run had 224 passes, 11 failures and 1 error; the `pose-mcp` run had 221, 11 and 1.\n- **Causes seen:** the messages include a network 403, ownership refusals on `/home` and `/var/tmp`, refused delegation, runtime start failures and a 600s timeout. Not every message identifies its cause.\n- **Baseline comparison:** `go test ./...` listed the same failing tests on the reviewed code and with this spec's files reverted. I skipped one hanging test in both runs. I therefore don't attribute the failures to this change.\n- **Sealed evidence:** it shows a pass.\n\n## Previous findings\n- **Fixed:** the two round 2 blockers. For R2-N10, 8 of 8 same-second rewrites now match plain `git diff`, and its new test fails when the timestamp fix is removed. For R2-N11, reads work without an index file.\n- **Partial:** R1-N9 and R2-N13.\n- **Not fixed:** R2-N12, which the spec tracks as a follow-up.\n\n## Remaining findings (all low, none blocking)\n\n| ID | Location (`pose-mcp/internal/…`) | Problem |\n|----|----------|---------|\n| N14 | `cli/check.go:1141` | A failed index read is still skipped silently, and one Git call has no time limit. |\n| N15 | `pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go:38` | With a split index, the shared index file's timestamp still changes. |\n| N16 | `cli/validate_reads_index_test.go:80` | Some cases and the ledger reader are still missing from the tests. |\n| N17 | `pose/git_worktree_reads.go:43` | The index size and type check isn't enforced on the bytes actually read (from reading the code, not reproduced). |\n\n## Other checks\n- `go vet` and the focused tests passed.\n- On an installed test project, `check`, `validate` and `report --since` left `.git/index` unchanged. That project matched no validation modules.\n- `artifact-check` and `surface-check` exited 0. `review-check` and `closeout-check` exited 1, as expected before an attestation.\n- I didn't run the non-Linux code.\n- `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal both exited 0 inside the sandbox.\n\nAll criteria are marked passed. `review draft-check` accepts the draft below.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n \"findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"N14\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/check.go\",\"line\":1141,\"summary\":\"Remainder of R2-N13: when the index cannot be located or read, the ready-transition read still drops the diff silently, and the rev-parse in ReadOnlyIndex (git_worktree_reads.go:26) runs without a deadline, outside the 30 second bound of reviewHistoryGit.\",\"action\":\"Report the failed ready-transition diff and run the index lookup under the caller's context.\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N15\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads_linux.go\",\"line\":38,\"summary\":\"R2-N12 remains: in a split-index repository the read-only diff moves the modification time of .git/sharedindex.<hash>, reproduced again. The spec records it as an open follow-up. Whether the governed read view reports it was not tested.\",\"action\":\"Keep a split-index read from touching the shared index time, as the spec follow-up states.\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N16\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_reads_index_test.go\",\"line\":80,\"summary\":\"Remainder of R1-N9: the CLI regression and concurrency tests do not run the review history ledger reader, and the equivalence test has no unmerged, range-base or dirty-submodule case. Overlay probes of those states matched the plain diff.\",\"action\":\"Add the ledger reader to the concurrency test and the three states to the equivalence test.\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"},\n  {\"id\":\"N17\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_worktree_reads.go\",\"line\":43,\"summary\":\"The regular-file and size bound is checked with Lstat and then the index is read with an unbounded os.ReadFile, replacing the earlier same-file, limited read. A file swapped between the two calls escapes the bound. Established by reading the code; it needs a writer inside .git and was not reproduced.\",\"action\":\"Read the index through an opened, same-file-checked, limited reader.\",\"owner\":\"pose-maintainers\",\"review_by\":\"2026-12-26\"}\n ],\n \"prior_findings\": [\n  {\"id\":\"R1-N9\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"git_worktree_reads_test.go adds a racily clean case and validate_reads_index_test.go:126 a missing-index case, but there is still no unmerged, range-base or dirty-submodule case and the CLI tests do not run the ledger reader. Carried as N16.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N10\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe TestProbeRacyDefault: 8 of 8 same-second rewrites matched the plain diff. TestReadOnlyIndexDiffSeesARacilyCleanEntry passed, and failed when an overlay removed the timestamp copy. git_worktree_reads_other.go sets the time with os.Chtimes (read, not run).\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N11\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"check.go:1138 applies the read-only index to diff only, report.go runs status plainly, and git_worktree_reads.go:32 reads plainly without an index. TestValidationReadsAnswerWithoutAnIndex passed; a probe matched the plain diff with no index and left it absent.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N12\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"Overlay probe TestProbeSplit: the shared index modification time still moved around RawGitDiffReadOnly. The spec lists it as an open follow-up. Carried as N15.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"R2-N13\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"validate_scope.go:109 now keeps the cause and git_worktree_reads.go reports its own index errors. check.go:1141 still continues silently and the rev-parse at git_worktree_reads.go:26 still has no deadline. Carried as N14.\"}\n ],\n \"sweep\": \"This round found no blocking code defect; the decision is changes-requested only because the required validate tool did not pass in the review sandbox, so an approval cannot be recorded truthfully. Read the round 3 diff and the subject's files: check.go, report.go, validate_scope.go, the four git_worktree_reads files, review_attempt_ledger.go, git_snapshot_integrity.go, both tests and the spec. Ran go vet, focused tests and a mutation of the timestamp copy. Overlay probes covered racy entries, a missing and a symlinked index, split index, a concurrent git add writer, submodule, symlink, directory replacement, range, subdirectory and conflict reads. End to end on an installed fixture with stale stats, check --strict, validate, validate --changed-from and report --since left .git/index byte-identical with the same time (the fixture matched no validation modules). Ran every planned pose tool, and go test ./... on the head and with this spec's files overlaid to their 9b5cf507 versions, skipping one hanging test in both. Not exercised: non-Linux code at runtime, a host without /proc, Git older than 2.31. report --since still passes its value to git unvalidated, as before this change.\",\n \"criteria\": [\n  {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Material assumptions: Git skips a refresh whose lock cannot be made, and trusts stat only for files older than the index. Both were verified by tests, the mutation and probes on this Linux Git. L2 is an accepted risk; /proc availability, Git 2.31 or newer and non-Linux runtime behavior remain unverified.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\"},\n  {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/machine-channel-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No command, flag, record or MCP schema changes. Probes show the diffs answer as the plain diff, including a missing or symlinked index and range bases, so the round 2 differences are gone.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-b76113f0017ed5dd\",\"rationale\":\"The cause is a stat refresh written under .git. Optional locks in gitCommandContext cover status (R1), and the diff reads a memfd whose lock cannot be created while keeping the index time (D1); D2 justifies testing the reads. The end-to-end probe left the index unchanged. The design delta has no structural deltas to map.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-b76113f0017ed5dd\",\"rationale\":\"No command, flag or template changes, so no operational document or scaffold needs an edit. D1, the execution log and the follow-up match the round 3 code.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Scope selection now carries the cause and index errors name the repository and the failure. The silent skip in check and the missing deadline are low and tracked in N14.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n  {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-b76113f0017ed5dd\",\"rationale\":\"The ten subject code files match the spec's artifact list and affected areas with no unrelated behaviour; artifact-check --strict exited 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions keep their validation, the redirecting Git environment stays stripped before the private index variable is added, the memfd creates no file, and the ledger sees racy and conflicting changes. The bound check gap is low and tracked in N17.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-b76113f0017ed5dd\",\"rationale\":\"Locks alone do not stop git diff writing and a temporary copy creates files, so an unlockable memfd over the unchanged diff is the smallest sufficient approach found, with no speculative extension. It becomes invalid if Git stops skipping a failed refresh lock or /proc is unavailable.\"}\n ],\n \"tools\": [\n  {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-b76113f0017ed5dd\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/git-status-clean-git-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; three medium unconsumed HTTP provider gaps unrelated to these files.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; the scan reports itself incomplete for two unreadable specs.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\",\"rationale\":\"Needs a completed review; it exited 1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-reads-leave-the-index-alone\",\"rationale\":\"Needs this review's attestation; it exited 1.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n  {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\",\"rationale\":\"surface-check --strict exited 0.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The run in this review sandbox exited 1: 224 pass, 11 fail, 1 error. A separate go test ./... listed the same failing tests on the head and with this spec's files reverted, and visible messages show ownership, network and delegation refusals, so the failures are not attributed to this change. The cited ref is the sealed pass, not this run.\"},\n  {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The module run in this review sandbox exited 1: 221 pass, 11 fail, 1 error, with the same failing step names; same baseline comparison. The cited ref is the sealed pass, not this run.\"}\n ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1651,"type":"result","duration_ms":101387,"uuid":"716be001-41e9-43f2-bdb8-7205e983a2ef","ttft_stream_ms":915,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":915,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":2,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":16849,"cacheReadInputTokens":1441746,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23112,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4051365999999